A||||21||OzFiero||What's the good oil ?||||5||
Z||000000||OzFiero||01-22-2001||10:39 PM||||Before I bought my Formula I heard that the bottom end of the 2.8 was weak so I switched to Mobil 1(5w-50) to try and preserve it. I noticed that the oil pressure went up about 5 psi after the switch . Seems  to have worked so far although lots of other things have broken. Synthetic oil costs $10/litre here vs. $2.50/litre for mineral based oil. Do you think it's really worth the extra money ? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||01-22-2001||10:59 PM||||Considering the cost of a rebuilt 2.8, that's pocket change.  I'm building a 3.1, and it's costing me over 1,000 bucks even with me having some of the parts already.  When my new motor has made it through it's break-in period, it's going to run nothing but Redline or Mobile 1.  And never use Champion oil... I wouldn't put that oil in my dogs a$$!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||G-Nasty||01-23-2001||12:16 AM||||Mobil one was good until the tri-synthetic. I will only use Castrol 5-50 synthetic. This is far better than both redline, amsoil and Mobil 1...quit watching speedvision.<BR>Do not use duralube or slick 50 and others. That stuff cakes up on top of your pistons-trust me I've seen it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-23-2001||12:41 AM||||Castor oil is good for getting Champion spark plugs <B>out</B> of my dogs ass...<P>Do they have Wal-Mart in Australia?||||reg||1
Z||000004||RaeQwan||01-23-2001||02:23 AM||||Despite what you think, you're gonna have a time getting a spark plug up ya dogs rear... no matter what type of oil ya use. Just somethings that are better left to now even being thought about hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Champ plugs can be used to twart off unexpected trick or treaters..  gaw darn pesky ole ppl.. get away from my house<P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||LarryB||01-23-2001||02:40 AM||||Castrol Synthetic is "synthetic" because a marketing group decided to more liberally apply the term 'syntheric'.  Syntec is described as a modified (the technical term is hydroprocessed) mineral oil, i.e. you can make a case that it's a natural oil that has been tweaked. <P>Doesn't mean that Castrol Syntec is an inferior product, just that the argument that Mobil 1 is a synthetic is less controversial than the one for Castrol.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||01-23-2001||09:19 AM||||Castrol Syntec isn't a full synthetic like Mobil 1.  <P>Champion oil sometimes comes out of my dogs ass when he eats table food, I give him some Mobil 1 and he perks right back up<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000007||Tigger||01-23-2001||09:48 AM||||Oz Welcome to the Forum.<P>I've had good luck with non-synthetics but I've heard lots of people say it's worth the money to use synthetic motor oils.  You'd have to check the labels, but I believe you can get up to twice the distance on synthetic motor oil.<P>stimpy, Wal-Mart in Austrailia is called Mal-Wart.  I think down under W's and M's get flipped, don't they?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Got2manyfieros||01-23-2001||10:15 AM||||Well, I like to use 2 quarts of mobile 1 10w-30, and use penzoil 10w-30 for the remainder.  5w-30 is a bit too light in my opinion, and I opt for the partial synthetic because sometimes when you switch a car from non-synthetic to straight synthetic, the engine becomes "unhappy".<P>Also, castrol is the motor oil equivolent of that cheap vodka that still has the chunks of potatoe in the bottom...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Richard Parnell||01-23-2001||01:34 PM||||Castrol is the oil that caused the problems that I mention in another thread.  Way too thin for the warm temps here.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||01-23-2001||02:26 PM||||I've been using 5-30 in my 2.8 since new Quaker State, Pennzoil, Mobil or what ever was on sale. 3000 mile oil changes.  No oil consumption problems. The only problem has been oil sending unit.  It's been replace 3x in 14 years.||||reg||3
