Z||000020||rogergarrison||02-03-2001||03:24 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>If synthetic oils were really that much better,the manufacturers would use it to cut down on warranty claims;they don't.Never mix oils,they can do some pretty strange things,leave some wierd deposits.<BR>I've used Kendall 20/50 for around 20 years,and have had no oil related failures.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>in case u havent noticed, manufactures do nothing to help make stuff last longer than warranty. If they did they couldnt sell you more new parts. They dont make that much off of selling you the car, but they kill you on replacement parts. 60 Minutes did a show on that once, took the price of a new Maverick and compared it to what it would cost (not including any labor) to replace every part. It went from like $7,000 for the new car to $40,000 for the total of the parts in 1976. I wish theyd do that again, like to see how it compares to today.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||1
